      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T13:31:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes this needs to clear the padding, and I think clear everything within the inset as well.\n\nWhen uploading the full pixmap to an atlas texture, we need the padding to have been initialized to zero so that texture filtering that\u0027s clamped to the padding is guaranteed to evaluate to the outer coverage (most of the time that should be 0, but for difference clips it should be 1).\n\nI think that when we call the drawShape() functions for regular raster atlas draws, it is implicitly assuming things started at 0. I didn\u0027t spot a call to RasterMaskHelper::clear.\n\nBut the clip atlas manager does use clear, in which case this sk_bzero is unnecessary. However, I think there is a separate issue with the clip atlas manager\u0027s changes because it would not always just clear to zero. When doing a single difference clip, I believe when it cleared to #FF, that would impact the padding pixels of the auto pixmap storage and so then clamped sampling would return full coverage like you\u0027d expect for an inverted fill.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "4357b0495547f4653f3de1ada1abc2001af0aafd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
